& [Problem] is one contained authority-generation mismatch
  + current machine and topology receipt forms reject quiescent_double_inventory and consistency
  + preserved scanner formation still names both
  + implicit child-to-parent reinterpretation is forbidden
  + no runtime exists, so no data migration or consumer compatibility path is needed

& [Supersession] is explicit and narrow
  + prior formation signature 040c8eb3-4c55-42c7-b731-f1223fb6b05f remains immutable historical authority
  + its RacePolicy strength quiescent_double_inventory is superseded
  + its ReceiptContract field consistency and value quiescent_double_inventory are superseded
  + its informal whole-root repetition is refined into the exact dual-acquisition conjunction below
  + every other prior scanner formation clause is inherited unless this canonical expressly changes it
  + no implementation or execution signature is superseded because none exists

& [ProfileBinding] is exact
  + scanner observation profile remains cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + machine forms dependency is cantor-phase3-machine-forms/0.2
  + topology forms dependency is cantor-phase3-topology-forms/0.3
  + topology receipt dependency is cantor-phase3-topology-receipt/0.3
  + formation revision profile is cantor-phase3-topology-scanner-formation-consistency-evidence-reconciliation/0.1
  + scanner profile continuity does not claim executable availability

& [CurrentVocabulary] is exact
  + evidence type is InventoryConsistencyEvidence
  + selected future-issued grade is NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + exact serialized token is non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal
  + receipt field is consistency_evidence
  + OsSnapshotProven remains inadmissible under topology receipt 0.3
  + quiescent_double_inventory and consistency are historical only and have no current formation alias

& [ActualAcquisition] is a future separately authorized event
  + created only by a physical producer under later M2C authority
  + owns stable acquisition identity and complete producer lineage
  + completes the full inherited scanner traversal and policy contract
  + pure supplied data, enum construction, receipt construction, and validation cannot create it

& [DualAcquisitionCardinality] is exact
  + exactly two acquisition roles support the selected evidence construction
  + FirstAcquisition and SecondAcquisition identities are distinct
  + each is independently actual and complete
  + neither may borrow completeness or lineage from the other
  + duplicate references, copied carriers, or one event in two roles deny construction

& [CausalOrder] is exact and clock neutral
  + FirstAcquisition.Completion strictly precedes SecondAcquisition.Start
  + first and second are established by this relation rather than caller names
  + left and right reconciliation operands have no inherent temporal meaning
  + no clock API, tick representation, duration, or read operation is authorized here
  + later M2C source must select and prove a bounded representation for this relation

& [CommonScope] is a complete exact product
  + candidate root reference
  + strong root identity
  + canonical root volume-GUID path
  + scanner observation profile
  + current machine and topology forms profiles
  + ordered observation encoding profile
  + every ScanLimits field
  + closed scanner and policy digest
  + predecessor admission receipt identity
  + reconciliation comparison scope
  + every coordinate is present and equal; omission is never wildcard or default

& [IndependentCarrierLineage] is mandatory
  + each acquisition retains its own complete root and entry observation ancestry
  + each acquisition retains its own current-valid supplied inventory assembly carrier
  + each acquisition retains its own current-valid ordered digest carrier
  + digest bytes alone are insufficient
  + one mutable or aliased carrier cannot serve both roles

& [ReconciliationDependency] is current and subordinate
  + use exact signed WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliation authority
  + supply exactly two complete current carriers
  + independently rederive both carriers under current rules
  + validate exact reconciliation profile and complete common scope
  + require disposition Equal
  + Different denies evidence construction without proving malicious or physical change
  + Equal is necessary and does not substitute for acquisition, order, completeness, scope, or issuer authority

& [EvidenceMeaning] is the complete conjunction
  + two distinct actual complete acquisitions
  + exact FirstCompletion-before-SecondStart causal relation
  + exact complete common scope
  + independent complete current carrier lineages
  + current exact-scope reconciliation Equal
  + future separately authorized evidence constructor and issuer
  + no conjunct may be inferred from another

& [NonAtomicBoundary] is mandatory
  + no snapshot, transaction, tree lock, indivisible acquisition, or uninterrupted unchanged interval
  + no denial of intermediate change-and-restore
  + no denial of change after the second acquisition
  + no denial of external writers
  + no present-state, quiescence, stability, immutability, safety, or freshness claim beyond separately proven receipt relations

& [ReceiptFormBoundary] is pure
  + TopologyReceipt 0.3 may structurally carry consistency_evidence NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + current validation proves schema and internal relation coherence only
  + public construction, serialization, decoding, or validation is not evidence derivation
  + valid form is not issued receipt and not consumer acceptance

& [FutureIssuanceBoundary] is formed but inactive
  + later separately signed issuer binds the complete evidence conjunction to exact receipt bytes
  + issuer also binds predecessor, root, policy, scanner, nonce, inventory, counts, issue, and freshness claims
  + issuer failure releases no partial authoritative receipt
  + this canonical adds no issuer type, API, key, signer, constructor, or operation

& [FutureConsumptionBoundary] is deferred
  + later M2E consumer verifies issuer, evidence lineage, receipt integrity, freshness, exact scope, and single use
  + work-packet construction and mutation admission follow only separate consumer success
  + this canonical adds no ledger, state, clock read, work packet, or admission operation

& [InheritedFormation] remains mandatory
  + exact input validation before observation
  + deterministic no-follow entry-before-descent traversal
  + strong identity, hard-link, duplicate-identity, and scan-local lifetime rules
  + complete stream and closed attribute policies
  + nested Git, submodule, sparse, control-state, and predecessor drift rejection
  + entry, depth, path, file, total, stream, deadline, and memory limits
  + typed fail-closed platform, access, absence, race, limit, path, alias, stream, attribute, Git, and OS faults
  + private RAII handles and narrow read-only Windows seam as unimplemented formation
  + separate M2A, M2B, M2C, M2D, and M2E source and signature gates

& [ConceptualFailureRules] are fail closed
  + source, predecessor, or signature drift invalidates formation authority
  + missing, duplicate, unauthorized, incomplete, or malformed acquisition lineage denies evidence construction
  + missing, inverse, cyclic, ambiguous, or unproven causal order denies evidence construction
  + absent or unequal common-scope coordinate denies evidence construction
  + incomplete, stale, malformed, bare, or aliased carrier denies evidence construction
  + current reconciliation fault or Different denies evidence construction
  + valid form without complete derivation and issuer authority denies issuance
  + no fault coerces, migrates, retries, downgrades, or releases partial authoritative success

& [P3TSFR-001] requires exact source and predecessor preservation
& [P3TSFR-002] requires explicit formation supersession
& [P3TSFR-003] requires current vocabulary and profiles
& [P3TSFR-004] requires two distinct actual complete acquisition lineages
& [P3TSFR-005] requires exact causal order
